1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. c3 d5 4. Qa4 f6 5. Bb5 Nge7 6. d3 (6. exd5 {is inferior
because of} Qxd5 7. O-O Bd7 {(Best)} 8. d4 exd4 9. cxd4 Ne5 {- the latter
excellent move was first played by Chigorin and with one stroke develops
Black's forces, and leaves White with an isolated pawn, for White's best reply
is} 10. Bxd7+ Qxd7 11. Qb3 Nxf3+ 12. Qxf3 O-O-O 13. Nc3 Nf5 {, etc. (Hoffer,
The Field)}) 6... dxe4 (6... Be6 {is considered better these days - JS}) 7.
dxe4 Bd7 8. Qc2 Nc8 9. Be3 Be7 10. Bc4 {A useless move, as the bishop cannot
maintain itself on the diagonal.} Na5 11. Bb3 ({We would not now give up the
bishop for the knight. Had White played} 11. Bd3 {or 11 Be2, the knight would
be out of play at a5.}) 11... Nb6 12. Qe2 Nxb3 13. axb3 O-O 14. Nbd2 Be6 15.
Rd1 Qe8 16. O-O Qf7 17. c4 Nd7 18. Nh4 Rfd8 19. f4 exf4 20. Bxf4 c6 21. Nf5 Nc5
22. Rf3 ({Stockfish 16:} 22. Nxe7+ Qxe7 23. e5 $11) 22... Rd7 23. Rg3 Bxf5 24.
exf5 Rad8 25. Rf1 Nd3 26. Ne4 Bb4 27. Bh6 ({Here White could have simplified
the game, and got rid of the opponent's well-posted knight, by} 27. Bc7 Rxc7
28. Rxd3 {, etc.}) 27... Bf8 28. Bc1 Kh8 29. Be3 b6 30. Nc3 Bb4 31. Kh1 Qe7 32.
Bg1 ({Giving up a pawn as a lesser evil. The alternative would have been} 32.
Nd5 cxd5 33. Qxd3 dxc4 34. Qxc4 {, with numerical equality, but inferior
position}) ({or} 32. Bc1 Nxc1 33. Qxe7 Bxe7 34. Rxc1 Rd2 35. Re3 Bb4 {, with
advantage.}) 32... Qxe2 33. Nxe2 Nxb2 34. Nc3 Bxc3 35. Rxc3 Rd1 36. Rxd1 Rxd1
37. Re3 h6 38. Re7 (38. Re8+ {would have been better, as the sequel will show.}
) 38... a6 ({Stockfish 16:} 38... Nd3 39. h3 Ra1 $19) 39. Ra7 Nd3 40. h3 Ra1
41. Kh2 b5 42. cxb5 cxb5 43. Ra8+ {Had the Black king been at h7, if White had
checked as pointed out [at move 38], he could now have played 43 Bd4 Ne5 44
Bxe5 fxe5 45 f6, etc.} Kh7 44. Ra7 Ra2 45. Bd4 {Too late.} Nf4 46. Bxf6 Rxg2+
47. Kh1 Rg3 48. Be5 Rxh3+ 49. Kg1 Nh5 50. f6 Rf3 51. fxg7 Rf5 52. Bd4 Rg5+ 53.
Kf2 Nxg7 54. Rxa6 {There is a remote chance of drawing the game, had White
taken the knight first.} Nf5 55. Bc5 ({Stockfish 16:} 55. Be5 $11) 55... h5 56.
Rb6 h4 57. Rb7+ Kg6 58. Rxb5 h3 59. Ra5 $4 ({Stockfish 16:} 59. Rb6+ $1 Kh5 60.
Bd6 $11) 59... h2 $19 60. Ra1 Ng3 {Mr. Wainwright played the whole game in
capital style. Source: The Field - Saturday 26 July 1890} 0-1

