1. e4 c6 {This move was introduced by the late Herr Kann, of Pest.
Theoretically it should be incorrect, because it prevents the Q Kt developing
upon its natural square. The defence has, nevertheless, proved itself to be
safe, but dull. (The Field)} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 g6 4. Be3 Bg7 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Be2
Nf6 7. e5 Nfd7 8. Qd2 f6 9. Bh6 O-O 10. Bxg7 Kxg7 11. exf6+ exf6 12. O-O f5 13.
